@*
    Literal routes (/blog, /projects/{slug}, …) out-rank ContentPage's "/{*path}" catch-all,
    because Blazor prefers literal segments over a catch-all parameter. That precedence is the
    single riskiest assumption in this design, so it is pinned by an integration test.

    NotFoundPage is what a component reaches by calling NavigationManager.NotFound(). Blazor's
    static SSR discards the output of a component that sets a 404 itself, so "render the 404
    page" has to go through the Router rather than through a child component.
*@
<Router AppAssembly="typeof(Program).Assembly" NotFoundPage="typeof(Pages.NotFoundPage)">
    <Found Context="routeData">
        <RouteView RouteData="routeData" DefaultLayout="typeof(MainLayout)" />
    </Found>
</Router>
